d 'KSMMD': module to perform Weighted k-sample distributional test combining Kolmogorov-Smirnov (Kiefer's T) and Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD via Random Fourier Features)
d
d	ksmmd tests whether k >= 2 groups (named by by()) come from
d the same distribution of varname, computing two test statistics  
d  from a single permutation resample:	      o a k-sample
d generalization of the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test (Kiefer's T --
d Kiefer 1959), the same statistic kstest (Ariel	    Linden,
d SSC s459801) computes, but reimplemented here so that varname is
d sorted once (not re-sorted on every		 permutation) --
d see Remarks: why reimplement kstest.	      o a k-sample
d generalization of the Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD -- Gretton et
d al. 2012) with an RBF kernel, approximated		via Random
d Fourier Features (Rahimi & Recht 2007) so it stays tractable at
d survey-sized n (~10^5), unlike mmd_2s 	   (Boston College
d SSC s459820), which only compares 2 groups with an exact O(N^2)
d kernel. 
d
d KW: distributions test
d KW: k-sample
d KW: KS test
d
d Requires: Stata version 11
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260917
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email talaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f ksmmd.ado
f ksmmd.sthlp
f ksmmd_es.sthlp
